<section class="product-roadmap">
  <h2 class="product-section-title">How to get in</h2>
  <ol class="product-roadmap-list">
    <li class="product-roadmap-item">
      <p class="product-roadmap-phase">Step 1</p>
      <h3 class="product-roadmap-title">Join the closed beta</h3>
      <p class="product-roadmap-desc">
        Leave your email above and we'll send your invite when there's room. We let people in a few at a time, so this
        is the step that starts the clock. On iOS, use the email tied to your Apple account: the TestFlight invite
        goes to that address.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li class="product-roadmap-item">
      <p class="product-roadmap-phase">Step 2</p>
      <h3 class="product-roadmap-title">Install Guido from your invite</h3>
      <p class="product-roadmap-desc">
        On Android the invite points at the Google Play listing, which isn't public during the beta. On iOS we add
        you in App Store Connect and TestFlight emails you the build. Either way, install from the link we send rather
        than from a search.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li class="product-roadmap-item">
      <p class="product-roadmap-phase">Step 3</p>
      <h3 class="product-roadmap-title">Connect your sim</h3>
      <p class="product-roadmap-desc">
        Gran Turismo 7 has a telemetry switch in the game settings, and that is the whole setup. Le
        Mans Ultimate and the Assetto Corsa games go through Muretto instead, a small Windows tray
        app that reads the sim for Guido. The Get started tabs below cover your sim.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li class="product-roadmap-item">
      <p class="product-roadmap-phase">Step 4</p>
      <h3 class="product-roadmap-title">Mount the phone and launch</h3>
      <p class="product-roadmap-desc">
        Put the phone on the same home network, best mounted beside your wheel, and open Guido. It finds your
        sim session on the network by itself.
      </p>
    </li>
  </ol>
</section>

